  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nThe extended dry spell gradually comes to an end this week as\nupper level ridging drifts offshore beginning this weekend.\nUntil then, mostly quiet weather remains center stage of the\nforecast. Today will feature ample sunshine and temperatures\nresembling slightly warmer than climatological norms for this\ntime of year.\n\nUpstream, a cold front was marked from Wisconsin and down into\nthe Central Plains. This boundary is slated to pass through the\nforecast area Friday morning, prompting a brief period of\ndrizzle along the higher terrain. Otherwise, the rest of the\narea should remain uninterrupted by this weak frontal passage.\n\nThe start of the weekend continues to remain on track from\nprevious model cycles to be dry and warm. This should yield\npleasant conditions for Halloween activities Saturday evening.\nMain changes to the forecast noted previously is a slightly\ndelayed approach of rain spreading back into the area in\nresponse to an encroaching southern stream disturbance. Showers\nlook to now press in from the southwest towards the second half\nof the day Sunday, but once it does, an unsettled weather \npattern prevails into the start of next week.",
